		<section class="section">
			<SectionHeader Title="Known limits" Meta="THE DOCUMENTED GAPS" />
			<p class="page-hero__sub" style="margin-bottom: var(--space-md)">
				<strong>The verifyCommand trap.</strong> The update stage's verifyCommand can fail
				with a non-zero status: on a vendored-fork workspace the forks are not on the
				public registry, so a <code>verifyCommand: pnpm install</code> fails and the
				ledger records the failure - the documented cordis registry trap, the expected
				outcome, not a bug. Exit 127 (the runner unavailable) is non-fatal; any other
				failure fails the stage and counts toward the circuit breaker (
				<code>maxUpdateFailures</code>, default 3).
			</p>
			<p class="page-hero__sub" style="margin-bottom: var(--space-md)">
				<strong>The fixture paths.</strong> The live battery's fixture ledgers carry the
				neutralized display forms (<code>&lt;repo-root&gt;/</code>,{" "}
				<code>$DSH_HOME/</code>); the personal absolute paths exist only in the internal
				Boilerplate copies - never copy a live battery into a release archive as-is.
			</p>
